# blx r3 sets lr = BASE+5 (the next instruction, Thumb bit set) and then branches to r3.
# Nothing is lifted at 0x5001, so mt_dispatch stops with MT_TRAP_NO_FUNCTION at the blx
# (pc = BASE+2, detail = the target). The push before it has already run.
title: blx r3 to an address with no function stops with MT_TRAP_NO_FUNCTION at the call
ref: A8.8 BLX (register) T1: LR = (PC - 2)<31:1>:'1', BXWritePC(R[m]); A8.8 PUSH T1; ADR 0014 addendum (#35): a dispatch miss traps

[code]
80b5        push {r7, lr}
9847        blx r3
80bd        pop {r7, pc}

[in]
r3 = 0x5001
r7 = 0x7777

[out]
trap = no_function BASE+2 0x5001
r13 = SP0-8
r14 = BASE+5
word SP0-8 = 0x7777 RET
flags = ????
